  "verdict": "void",
  "section": "37",
  "quote": "A notice of termination need not be given if a landlord and a tenant have agreed to terminate a tenancy, unless the agreement to terminate was entered into when the tenancy agreement was entered into or as a condition of entering into the tenancy agreement, in which case the agreement to terminate is void and a landlord or a tenant shall not give a notice of termination when the tenancy agreement is entered into or as a condition of entering into the tenancy agreement and any such notice is void.",
  "reason": "Section 37 of the Act explicitly prohibits a tenant or landlord from giving a notice of termination at the time the tenancy agreement is entered into or as a condition of entering into it. Under section 4(1), any provision in a tenancy agreement that conflicts with the Act is void."
}

